    'Frederik VI (Frederiksberg)': 'Frederiksberg\'s living room since 1973, on tree-lined Frederiksberg Allé, equal parts proper brown pub and lunch spot. Lazy afternoon pints slide into lively evenings, with a hidden summer back garden most visitors never find.',
    'Hviids Vinstue (Indre By)': 'Copenhagen\'s oldest bar, established 1723 on Kongens Nytorv, with a strict no-music policy so conversation is the only soundtrack. Famous for its November gløgg and 27 Danish beers under candlelit, dark-wood ceilings.',
    'Café Haraldsborg (Islands Brygge)': 'About as typical a Danish brown pub as exists, run by a husband-and-wife team with friendly regulars on Islands Brygge. Smoking permitted, retro beer signage and low lamps, and a cosy calm that sparks to life at night.',
    'Floss (Indre By)': 'A late-night stalwart on Larsbjørnsstræde with punk attitude, from the smoky ground-floor bar to a graffiti-strewn basement games room. Cheap, loud, and gloriously unpretentious in the heart of the Latin Quarter.',
