    'Hisense C2 Ultra':
      "Tom's Guide's best projector of 2026, a 3,000-lumen triple-laser 4K unit on a motorized gimbal stand. Reviewers say the image holds up even in lit rooms, with ultra-precise color and strong contrast.",
    'Sony Bravia Projector 9':
      "Sony's $31,998 flagship brings native 4K SXRD, 3,400 laser lumens, and the XR processor from Bravia TVs. Projector Reviews places it at the very top of the premium tier.",
    'JVC DLA-NZ800':
      "The more attainable of JVC's 8K e-shiftX pair and TechRadar's 8K pick at $15,999 launch. D-ILA native contrast that LCD and DLP rivals simply cannot match.",
    'Epson Pro Cinema LS9000':
      "Epson's 2025 laser took both What Hi-Fi's premium slot and TechRadar's home theater slot. Much of the LS12000 formula in a smaller chassis for $3,999.",
    'JVC DLA-NZ500':
      "JVC's most affordable native 4K D-ILA laser, a ProjectorCentral Editor's Choice, with 40,000:1 native contrast at $5,999.95. The entry ticket to true JVC black levels.",
    'BenQ TH671ST':
      "RTINGS' budget pick: a 1080p short-throw that fills 100 inches from five feet. With 675 Amazon ratings at 4.5 stars, buyers love it for gaming and bright rooms.",
